{
  "title": "2026 年企业 LLM Agent 平台选型",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Executive Summary",
      "paragraph": "RefractRouter v0.1 将选型问题定义为：为固定任务 DAG 的逐节点模型选择挑选执行基座。候选集收敛为 LangGraph、DeepAgents、Pydantic AI 与 DeepSeek Harness。LangGraph 作为底层图状态机基座提供显式节点、边、持久状态与检查点 [source_002]；DeepAgents 是构建于 LangGraph 之上的 LangChain 封装 [source_001]；Pydantic AI 提供类型化工具与结构化输出 [source_003]；DSH 保留给外层验证环境 [source_004]。基准需报告质量、成本与关键路径延迟 [source_007]。"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Background",
      "paragraph": "现有 LLM 路由研究多为整个请求选择单一模型，而 RefractRouter 研究是否可为任务 DAG 中每个节点分别选择模型，以改善质量-成本-延迟帕累托前沿 [source_005]。静态任务分解属于应用层，路由器接收 DAG 作为输入并聚焦逐节点模型选择，动态重拆分推迟到节点级路由验证之后 [source_006]。"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Selection Criteria",
      "paragraph": "有用的路由基准要求固定任务 DAG、多个候选模型、逐节点与逐任务评分、成本核算以及关键路径延迟，且首个基准应保持小规模以便复现 [source_007]。v0.1 评分规则对需求覆盖、证据准确性、分析深度、结构与可读性以及 HTML 有效性加权，评分提示与规则版本须随运行记录一起版本化 [source_008]。"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Platform Comparison",
      "paragraph": "LangGraph 提供显式节点、边、持久状态与检查点，是承载固定 DAG 并保留中间状态重估路由决策所需的最小原语，但不提供智能体语义、规划或工具类型 [source_002]。DeepAgents 构建于 LangGraph，增加规划、子智能体、文件系统抽象与人机协同控制，v0.1 应保留其易用性但禁用自主规划与动态子智能体生成 [source_001]。Pydantic AI 提供类型化工具定义与结构化模型输出，仅在结构化输出成为瓶颈时引入 [source_003]。DSH 的智能体循环本身是插件，将路由循环插入 DSH 会混淆控制流并掩盖质量与成本归因，故保留给外层验证环境 [source_004]。"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Risks",
      "paragraph": "更丰富的封装如 DeepAgents 与 DSH 提升能力，但也为质量-成本-延迟基准引入混淆因素 [source_007]。若将 DSH 用于核心路由循环，会混淆两条控制流并掩盖质量与成本归因 [source_004]。过早引入 Pydantic AI 作为核心依赖会增加模式维护开销，而节点级路由尚未验证 [source_003]。DeepAgents 的自主规划与动态子智能体生成可能扰动逐节点路由实验 [source_001]。"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Conclusion",
      "paragraph": "v0.1 技术栈应优先选择最小、确定性的基座：以 LangGraph 作为核心执行基座 [source_002]，保留 DeepAgents 的易用性但禁用自主特性 [source_001]，仅在结构化输出成为瓶颈时引入 Pydantic AI [source_003]，并将 DSH 保留给外层验证环境 [source_004]。该取舍在能力与实验隔离之间取得平衡，使质量-成本-延迟基准的归因保持清晰 [source_007]。"
    },
    {
      "heading": "References",
      "paragraph": "本文引用以下来源：DeepAgents [source_001]、LangGraph [source_002]、Pydantic AI [source_003]、DeepSeek Harness [source_004]、LLM routing research gap [source_005]、Task decomposition boundary [source_006]、Benchmark design [source_007]、Scoring rubric [source_008]。"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "source_id": "source_001",
      "title": "DeepAgents",
      "content_hash": "ed7d5a479cc077720b641eb8ecf4a25c3af32701fc8403138c57532c6dd03d39",
      "claim": "DeepAgents is a LangChain harness built on LangGraph, providing planning, sub-agents, a filesystem abstraction, and human-in-the-loop controls; for RefractRouter v0.1 it is useful as a fixed-DAG execution harness but its autonomous planning and dynamic sub-agent generation should remain disabled."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_002",
      "title": "LangGraph",
      "content_hash": "97960ed618df652ae16f900a1ea677e257684118f5eab68686b2f8713ae74960",
      "claim": "LangGraph is a graph state machine framework for complex workflows supporting explicit nodes, edges, durable state, and check-pointing, and RefractRouter uses it as the lower-level execution substrate for a fixed task DAG."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_003",
      "title": "Pydantic AI",
      "content_hash": "7edd7c4a831f8cb06e0c9fc8b17911818ad63ff686b7d7245b176c46a3cea42e",
      "claim": "Pydantic AI provides typed tool definitions and structured model outputs and is useful when strict schemas are required, but RefractRouter v0.1 does not need it as a core dependency unless structured-output parsing becomes a bottleneck."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_004",
      "title": "DeepSeek Harness",
      "content_hash": "b06d562fa3e636b8ffb02c1578e300033ae7f23672b90445a9489bbe65b57331",
      "claim": "DeepSeek Harness (DSH) is an agent harness where the agent loop itself is a plugin, and for RefractRouter v0.1 it is reserved for the outer validation environment rather than the core routing loop."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_005",
      "title": "LLM routing research gap",
      "content_hash": "418b6cda722a8338f10fa145fb4f4f5c3f188ff413651e4d73aa2949b4e07460",
      "claim": "Existing LLM routing work mostly selects one model for an entire request, whereas RefractRouter studies whether selecting a model separately for each node in a task DAG can improve the quality-cost-latency Pareto frontier."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_006",
      "title": "Task decomposition boundary",
      "content_hash": "96a837f9788f5d0c6d9ab2cc9633775c42dc5569afc70b1782dc1d6d7a198504",
      "claim": "Static task decomposition belongs to the application layer, so the router receives the DAG as input and focuses on per-node model selection, with dynamic re-splitting deferred until node-level routing is validated."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_007",
      "title": "Benchmark design",
      "content_hash": "03e9443028f0065ae41218c422efdcebe73225465468098c9ba49f03596be4d0",
      "claim": "A useful routing benchmark requires fixed task DAGs, multiple candidate models, per-node and per-task scoring, cost accounting, and critical-path latency, and the first benchmark should stay small enough to reproduce."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "source_008",
      "title": "Scoring rubric",
      "content_hash": "b669e75265f9d0997a8f62659ca6526b2911a6d4af1f2c9ed956870c166a816e",
      "claim": "The v0.1 scoring rubric weights requirement coverage, evidence accuracy, analysis depth, structure and readability, and HTML validity, and scoring prompts and rubric versions must be versioned with run records."
    }
  ]
}
